<article class="env-proposition" id="CD55">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/CD55">Proposition <span data-tag="CD55">2.4.7.9</span>.</a> Let $X \stackrel{p}{\rightarrow } Y \stackrel{q}{\rightarrow } S \times T$ satisfy the hypotheses of Proposition <a href="/tag/EB64" data-tag="EB64">2.4.7.6</a>. Suppose that $p$ is a cofibration. Then there exists a retraction $r: Y \rightarrow X$ $($as a map of simplicial sets <em>over</em> $S \times T$$)$ such that $r \circ p = \id _ X$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Lemma <a href="/tag/BDC7" data-tag="BDC7">2.4.7.8</a> in the case $A = X$, $B = Y$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>